<title>CANADA: Alberta Wheat Pool downgrades crop outlook on rain.</title>
<headline>Alberta Wheat Pool downgrades crop outlook on rain.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Alberta Wheat Pool said on Friday the number of its reporting stations rating soil moisture as excessive doubled since last week, leading to a downgrade of its crop outlook issued last week.</p>
<p>AWP's crop condition index of 100 represents optimal growing conditions while 50 represents average crop output.</p>
<p>CROPS			 CONDITIONS INDEX</p>
<p>				This Wk  Last Wk  June 27/96</p>
<p>Hard Red Spring Wheat   78	 80	 80</p>
<p>Can Prairie Spring Wheat76	 80	 80</p>
<p>Soft White Spring Wheat 69	 61	 68</p>
<p>Winter Wheat		66	 62	 60</p>
<p>Durum Wheat		 66	 67	 72</p>
<p>Oats			  73	 79	 80</p>
<p>Barley			76	 80	 80</p>
<p>Flax			  56	 71	 56</p>
<p>Canola			76	 77	 73</p>
<p>Fall Rye		    71	 68	 62</p>
<p>AVERAGE CROP CONDITION  76	 79	 79</p>
<p>((Gilbert Le Gras, Winnipeg Reuters bureau 204 947 3548))</p>
